From 18aa4f11841420da25fa72acc2a3f519d448a02f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Skynizz <182822215+Skynizz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 23:55:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/6] KRC-A: adaptive cells on SHaRC's table (parent per fine cell, statistical blend)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

- krcPropagate pass: each fine cell's frame sums also go to its parent, twice
  as large (bit 63 of the key).
- Moments per entry (frame-to-frame variance of the mean), at resolve time.
- Reading: James-Stein shrinkage towards the parent, with a relative tolerance.
- Bench: tech=krc, scale=, krctol=, krcdebug=.

